  "run_id": "bb050743b1",
  "final_message": "**Status:** Reproduced\n\n**Expected:** With `<BaseLayout><template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname>\u2026</template><SubComponent><template #title>\u2026</template><template #_duration>\u2026</template></SubComponent></BaseLayout>`, both `title` and `_duration` slot content render in `SubComponent` (as in 3.5.13).\n\n**Actual:** `title` renders, but `_duration` shows the slot's fallback content. Rendered HTML from the check: `<div><p>conditional</p><div class=\"ok\">title works</div><div class=\"fallback\">fallback _duration</div></div>`.\n\n**Trigger:** A component whose slots are compiled as dynamic (`v-if`, `v-for` or a `#[name]` on one of its `<template #slot>`s) and that has a child component with `_`-prefixed slot names in its default slot. The slot name does not have to exist in the parent. I tried these variants:\n- `v-if` sibling slot: fails.\n- Dynamic slot name sibling: fails.\n- `v-if` on the default slot itself: fails.\n- No conditional or dynamic sibling slot: works.\n- Non-underscore slot name next to the `v-if` slot: works.\n\n**Run:** `pnpm vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` (exits 1 now, asserts the report's expected output). The test compiles the report's templates at runtime, which uses the same slot transform as the playground SFCs.\n\n**Passes when:** I saw it pass in two cases.\n- A throwaway edit to `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` (filter only `_`, `__` and `$stable` instead of every `_`-prefixed key). It is reverted.\n- Published `vue@3.5.13` renders `<div><p>c</p><b>T</b><b>D_</b></div>` for the same template; `vue@3.5.14` renders `<i>fb-dur</i>` instead of `<b>D_</b>`.\n\n**Likely cause:** The parent's dynamic slot flag makes `renderSlot` create a BAIL fragment, so the child mounts with `optimized = false`. In that case `assignSlots` skips every key where `isInternalKey(key)` is true, and that check is `key[0] === '_'`. This drops user slots such as `_duration` along with the `_` compiler flag.\n\n**Artifacts:** `/work/runs/bb050743b1/repo/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` (new test). No production code was changed.\n",
  "run_command": "pnpm vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..01a55c6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@\n+import { createApp } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reproduces the report: <template #_name> slot content is ignored (fallback\n+// content is rendered instead) when the component that owns the slot is placed\n+// inside another component's default slot, next to a conditionally rendered\n+// <template v-if #slot> for that parent component.\n+describe('slot names starting with an underscore', () => {\n+  const SubComponent = {\n+    template: `\n+      <slot name=\"title\"><div class=\"fallback\">fallback title</div></slot>\n+      <slot name=\"_duration\"><div class=\"fallback\">fallback _duration</div></slot>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `\n+      <div>\n+        <slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot>\n+        <slot></slot>\n+      </div>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+\n+  function mountApp(template: string) {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    createApp({\n+      components: { SubComponent, BaseLayout },\n+      data: () => ({ anyConditionCheckHereWillDo: true }),\n+      template,\n+    }).mount(container)\n+    return container.innerHTML\n+  }\n+\n+  // exact structure from the report\n+  it('renders #_duration content as a child of a component with a conditional slot template', () => {\n+    const html = mountApp(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"anyConditionCheckHereWillDo\" #randomslotname>\n+          <p>conditional</p>\n+        </template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><div class=\"ok\">title works</div></template>\n+          <template #_duration><div class=\"ok\">_duration works</div></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>\n+    `)\n+    expect(html).toContain('title works')\n+    expect(html).toContain('_duration works')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('fallback')\n+  })\n+})\n"
}
